Command	                                                                                                   Use

pwd	                                                             Displays the present working directory.
ls	                                                             Lists files and directories in the current directory.
ls -l	                                                           Displays files in long listing format with permissions, size and ownership.
ls -la	                                                         Displays all files, including hidden files, in long listing format.
ls -lh	                                                         Displays file sizes in human-readable format.
ls -lah	                                                         Displays all files, including hidden files, with detailed and human-readable information.
mkdir	                                                           Creates a new directory.
cd	                                                             Changes the current working directory.
cd ..                                                            Moves to the parent directory.
echo "message"	                                                 Displays the specified message on the terminal.
touch File1.txt                   	                             Creates an empty file or updates its timestamp.
cat > file.txt	                                                 Creates a file and writes input into it by overwriting existing content.
cat >> file.txt	                                                 Appends new content to an existing file.
cat file.txt	                                                   Displays the contents of a file.
cat < file.txt	                                                 Reads file contents using input redirection.
cat File1.txt \| sort \| head -n 3	                             Sorts file contents and displays the first three lines.
cat File1.txt \| sort \| tail -n 3	                             Sorts file contents and displays the last three lines.
grep "operating" File1.txt	                                     Searches for the word "operating" in the specified file.
cp File1.txt File2.txt	                                         Copies the contents of one file into another file.
mv File1.txt File3.txt	                                         Moves or renames a file.
rm File1.txt error.txt	                                         Deletes the specified files.
rmdir directory	                                                 Removes an empty directory.
